id: public_forum
----
## A public forum on AI

In May 2026, we opened a public forum on the *Impact of AI on work* to all Californians. In the months to follow, thousands of people across the state gave us their thoughts by taking our survey. Some survey respondents later joined facilitated group discussions held on Zoom. They shared their own experiences, and listened to their peers. Then they refined gut reactions into concrete policy ideas.

Along the way, participants didn’t always agree. They debated how far to regulate, how proposals would be funded, and how the rules would be enforced.

One theme came up consistently: **We need humans in the AI policy loop**. Not only for how people use AI, but for how companies build it and laws govern it.

