## Ideas we heard

### First, from the survey

Our survey asked people what they’d like government to do about the impact of AI. We got a wide range of ideas for policies.
----
id: word_cloud
translator_note: "The phrases in the word cloud come from a data file. To show translated phrases, add a line `src: /public/data/<translated-file>.json` here once the data team has produced one; otherwise the English phrases are shown."
chart_alt: "Word cloud of the policy ideas raised in the survey, sized by how many people raised each one."
----

----
id: ranking
----
### Then from live discussions

The AI policy ideas below came from the 2-hour live discussions over Zoom. Participants refined their policy ideas and voted on what was most important.

We grouped what people said there into 26 distinct ideas. Then we ranked them according to:

- How often an idea came up across discussions (frequency), and
- How much support it drew when it did (how often it was a popular idea).
